    perf(client): one set of search tables a thread, not one a search
    
    A search clears what it reads (ttFlag gates the table; the move lists are
    written before they are read), so the searches of one thread share one set
    instead of allocating and zeroing 3.3 MB each think and review position.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011SfWVyoMjkEfNUzxfLRC8S

